# Day 3 – Task 1: Few-Shot Accuracy

## Objective
Classify 20 expense descriptions into six company expense categories using Zero-Shot and Few-Shot Prompting techniques.

## Tasks Performed
1. Created Zero-Shot prompts to classify expense descriptions without examples.
2. Created Few-Shot prompts using examples of previously classified expenses.
3. Tested both prompting techniques using Google Gemini.
4. Recorded the prompts, outputs, expected categories, and scores in Excel.
5. Compared the accuracy of both methods.

## Expense Categories
- CAPEX-IT
- OPEX-Welfare
- OPEX-Maintenance
- OPEX-Travel
- OPEX-Office
- OPEX-Training

## Accuracy Results

| Method | Correct Answers | Total Questions | Accuracy |
|---|---:|---:|---:|
| Zero-Shot | 18 | 20 | 90% |
| Few-Shot | 18 | 20 | 90% |

## Key Observations
- Both methods achieved 90% accuracy.
- Zero-Shot and Few-Shot each classified 18 expenses correctly.
- Q11 and Q12 were incorrectly classified by both methods.
- Few-Shot prompting did not improve accuracy in this experiment.

## Conclusion
Completed the expense classification experiment and compared Zero-Shot and Few-Shot Prompting using Google Gemini.

**Result:** Zero-Shot – 90%; Few-Shot – 90%.

